<title>RUSSIA: First Russian beet test avg weight 151 grams.</title>
<headline>First Russian beet test avg weight 151 grams.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's first sugar beet test did not provide data for sugar content but showed an average beet weight of a total 151 grams, the Rossakhsvyokla sugar beet producers' association said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It provided the following details:  </p>
<p>				  RUSSIAN SUGAR BEET TESTING</p>
<p>				 1st 1997 test     1st 1996 test</p>
<p> Avg sugar content	     n/a		  9.5</p>
<p> Beet weight (grams)	   151		  132</p>
<p>  stem				34		   30</p>
<p>  top				117		  102</p>
<p> Beets per hectare	   73,000		70,000</p>
<p>The test was conducted on July 1.</p>
<p>Russia will conduct its next test around July 10, with results available a few days later.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
